{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 02. Trajectory Continuous Segmentation & 120-Second Analysis Windowing\n",
    "\n",
    "**Project**: AI-Driven Predictive Geofencing and Trajectory Analysis for Proactive Safety Monitoring  \n",
    "**Stage**: Chunk 2 — Continuous Segmentation & 120-Second Windowing Exploration  \n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates and validates the trajectory segmentation and 120-second non-overlapping analysis windowing pipeline implemented in [`ml/src/trajectory.py`](../src/trajectory.py).\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Methodological Principle**: Source `.plt` files represent extended logging sessions that often span across hours or days of inactivity. Continuous segmentation splits trajectories on genuine inactivity gaps ($\Delta t > 300\\text{s}$) to avoid false movement interpolations, and partitions each continuous segment into non-overlapping 120-second analysis windows for later kinematic feature extraction."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import json\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "# Resolve paths dynamically\n",
    "NOTEBOOK_DIR = Path.cwd() if Path.cwd().name == \"notebooks\" else Path.cwd() / \"ml\" / \"notebooks\"\n",
    "PROCESSED_DIR = NOTEBOOK_DIR.parent / \"data\" / \"processed\"\n",
    "CANONICAL_PARQUET = PROCESSED_DIR / \"trajectories.parquet\"\n",
    "WINDOWS_PARQUET = PROCESSED_DIR / \"trajectory_windows.parquet\"\n",
    "REPORT_FILE = PROCESSED_DIR / \"segmentation_window_report.json\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Canonical Dataset:   {CANONICAL_PARQUET} (exists: {CANONICAL_PARQUET.exists()})\")\n",
    "print(f\"Windowed Dataset:    {WINDOWS_PARQUET} (exists: {WINDOWS_PARQUET.exists()})\")\n",
    "print(f\"Quality Report File: {REPORT_FILE} (exists: {REPORT_FILE.exists()})\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Load Segmentation & Window Quality Report"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if REPORT_FILE.exists():\n",
    "    with open(REPORT_FILE, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
    "        report = json.load(f)\n",
    "    print(\"=== Trajectory Segmentation & 120s Window Quality Report ===\\n\")\n",
    "    for k, v in report.items():\n",
    "        if isinstance(v, dict):\n",
    "            print(f\"\\n{k.upper()}:\")\n",
    "            for sub_k, sub_v in v.items():\n",
    "                print(f\"  {sub_k}: {sub_v}\")\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            print(f\"{k}: {v}\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Report not generated yet. Run `python ml/src/trajectory.py`.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Inspect Empirical Temporal Sampling Gap Distribution\n",
    "\n",
    "Why is $\\Delta T = 300\\text{s}$ (5 minutes) selected as the default continuous segmentation threshold?\n",
    "- In the canonical GeoLife dataset, **99.835%** of all valid consecutive fixes occur within $\\le 300$ seconds.\n",
    "- 300 seconds represents **2.5 full 120-second analysis windows**. An unobserved gap of $> 5$ minutes cannot be assumed to be continuous movement without introducing severe spatial interpolation distortion."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load a sample of canonical trajectories to inspect the gap distribution\n",
    "sample_df = pd.read_parquet(CANONICAL_PARQUET, columns=[\"trajectory_id\", \"timestamp\"]).head(500000)\n",
    "same_traj = sample_df[\"trajectory_id\"] == sample_df[\"trajectory_id\"].shift(1)\n",
    "diffs = (sample_df[\"timestamp\"] - sample_df[\"timestamp\"].shift(1)).dt.total_seconds().to_numpy()\n",
    "pos_diffs = diffs[same_traj & (diffs > 0)]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Analyzed {len(pos_diffs):,} positive interval transitions:\")\n",
    "print(pd.Series(pos_diffs).describe(percentiles=[0.5, 0.75, 0.9, 0.95, 0.99, 0.999]))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Load Windowed Parquet Dataset & Schema Inspection"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df_win = pd.read_parquet(WINDOWS_PARQUET)\n",
    "print(f\"Windowed Dataset Shape: {df_win.shape[0]:,} rows x {df_win.shape[1]} columns\")\n",
    "df_win.info()\n",
    "df_win.head(5)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Entity Cardinality: Trajectories, Segments, and Windows"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "num_trajs = df_win[\"trajectory_id\"].nunique()\n",
    "num_segs = df_win[\"segment_id\"].nunique()\n",
    "num_wins = df_win[\"window_id\"].dropna().nunique()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Source Trajectories:  {num_trajs:,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Continuous Segments:  {num_segs:,} (Ratio: {num_segs / num_trajs:.2f} segments per trajectory)\")\n",
    "print(f\"120s Analysis Windows: {num_wins:,} (Ratio: {num_wins / num_segs:.2f} windows per segment)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Full vs. Partial Windows Distribution"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "win_summary = df_win.groupby(\"window_id\")[\"is_full_window\"].first().value_counts()\n",
    "print(\"Window Type Breakdown:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Full 120s Windows:    {win_summary.get(True, 0):,} ({win_summary.get(True, 0) / len(win_summary) * 100:.2f}%)\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Partial Trailing:     {win_summary.get(False, 0):,} ({win_summary.get(False, 0) / len(win_summary) * 100:.2f}%)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Example: Continuous Segmentation across Large Temporal Gaps"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Find a trajectory that was segmented due to a large temporal gap\n",
    "multi_seg_trajs = df_win.groupby(\"trajectory_id\")[\"segment_id\"].nunique()\n",
    "example_traj_id = multi_seg_trajs[multi_seg_trajs > 1].index[0]\n",
    "sub_traj = df_win[df_win[\"trajectory_id\"] == example_traj_id].sort_values([\"timestamp\", \"subsecond_seq\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Trajectory {example_traj_id} contains {sub_traj['segment_id'].nunique()} continuous segments:\")\n",
    "for seg_id, grp in sub_traj.groupby(\"segment_id\", sort=False):\n",
    "    t_start = grp[\"timestamp\"].iloc[0]\n",
    "    t_end = grp[\"timestamp\"].iloc[-1]\n",
    "    dur = (t_end - t_start).total_seconds()\n",
    "    print(f\"  Segment {seg_id}: {len(grp)} pts | {t_start} -> {t_end} | Duration: {dur:.1f}s | Windows: {grp['window_id'].nunique()}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Example: 120-Second Analysis Windows within a Segment"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Inspect individual windows in a segment\n",
    "example_seg_id = sub_traj[\"segment_id\"].iloc[0]\n",
    "seg_data = sub_traj[sub_traj[\"segment_id\"] == example_seg_id]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"=== Window Breakdown for Segment {example_seg_id} ===\")\n",
    "for w_id, w_grp in seg_data.groupby(\"window_id\", sort=False):\n",
    "    t_start = w_grp[\"timestamp\"].iloc[0]\n",
    "    t_end = w_grp[\"timestamp\"].iloc[-1]\n",
    "    is_full = w_grp[\"is_full_window\"].iloc[0]\n",
    "    span = (t_end - t_start).total_seconds()\n",
    "    print(f\"  Window {w_id} ({'FULL' if is_full else 'PARTIAL'}): {len(w_grp)} pts | span: {span:.1f}s | {t_start} -> {t_end}\")\n"
   ]
  }
 ],
